🕵️ SBHunter — Smart Subdomain Hunter

A modern, fast, and user-friendly subdomain discovery tool.
Passive OSINT + active brute-force + wildcard detection + liveness verification (httpx) — all in one command.

🚀 Features
🔍 Amass (passive) runs automatically
🧩 All tool outputs are merged: subdomains/*.txt → unique → final.txt
🌐 Liveness verification: final.txt → httpx → final_alive.txt
🧠 Wildcard filter: automatically removes false positives
⚙️ Fallback mechanism: embedded dig loop if puredns/dnsx are missing
🎨 User-friendly interface: --pretty for colored, sectioned output
🧱 Continues even if some tools are missing: missing tools are reported and the pipeline proceeds
🧰 Number of supported tools: 11 — assetfinder, subfinder, sublist3r, chaos, findomain, amass, dnsx, puredns, httpx, ffuf, gobuster

📦 Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/serkanbenol/sbhunter.git
cd sbhunter
chmod +x sbhunter.py
```

Requirements (optional but recommended): amass, subfinder, assetfinder, findomain, chaos, dnsx, puredns, httpx, ffuf, gobuster

⚡️ Usage
Single domain:

```bash
./sbhunter.py -d example.com --auto --pretty
```

Domain list (one domain per line):

```bash
./sbhunter.py --auto -f targets.txt --pretty
```

Including brute-force:

```bash
./sbhunter.py -d example.com --auto --bruteforce --pretty
```

Amass active scan (optional, may take long):

```bash
./sbhunter.py -d example.com --auto --amass-active --pretty
```

Custom resolver (for fallback dig):

```bash
./sbhunter.py -d example.com --auto --resolver 8.8.8.8 --pretty
```

🔄 Workflow Stages
Subdomain Enumeration

assetfinder, sublist3r, subfinder, chaos, findomain, amass (passive)
(Optional) puredns, dnsx, or fallback dig loop
Overlay Prefix → generate new candidates using prefixes like vpn, sso, admin

Validation & Wildcard Filtering

VHOST & Dir Brute (optional, ffuf or gobuster)

Unique Merge → final.txt

HTTPX Alive Scan → final_alive.txt

Result Summary: colored, clean, readable output

